WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.023
Brring! The first bell rang, but nobody moved.

2
00:00:05.024 --> 00:00:09.065
Everyone around Ben was laughing hysterically at the poster.

3
00:00:09.066 --> 00:00:14.537
Ben couldn't help laughing too.

4
00:00:14.538 --> 00:00:19.989
Mr. Freaky looked ridiculous with big bushy whiskers under his noses.

5
00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.056
The Doppel Gang stood near the poster with Mog.

6
00:00:23.057 --> 00:00:26.062
Larry held a thick black marker.

7
00:00:26.063 --> 00:00:29.967
Ben had little doubt about who had drawn the mustache.

8
00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:34.007
Pixel snapped a few photos of the poster.

9
00:00:34.008 --> 00:00:39.906
Then he took some shots of the laughing students.

10
00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:44.563
"Fun scenes from Art Week," he said, floating toward Ben.

11
00:00:44.564 --> 00:00:48.123
"We can put these photos on the school website."

12
00:00:48.124 --> 00:00:52.517
"Um . . . I'm not sure Mr. Freaky will like that," Ben said.

13
00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:56.295
"But we'll find out in a second because here he comes!"

14
00:00:56.296 --> 00:01:02.047
"Students!" Mr. Freaky was racing toward the group, his arms flapping like mad.

15
00:01:02.048 --> 00:01:06.015
"Students! What is going on? The bell rang!

16
00:01:06.016 --> 00:01:11.035
Why aren't you in your classrooms?" His noses wiggled wildly.

17
00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:14.747
"What is Mr. Freaky wearing?" somebody said.

18
00:01:14.748 --> 00:01:17.558
Ben had been wondering the same thing.

19
00:01:17.559 --> 00:01:23.772
The school principal wore a suit, as usual, but over it was a strange-looking apron.

20
00:01:23.773 --> 00:01:27.321
And atop his head was a stranger-looking mask.

21
00:01:27.322 --> 00:01:35.248
"Is that a welder's mask?" Ben thought.

22
00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:39.992
The principal screeched to a halt as his eyes landed on the poster.

23
00:01:39.993 --> 00:01:43.092
A few monsters began tiptoeing away.

24
00:01:43.093 --> 00:01:47.145
For a second the hallway was completely silent.

25
00:01:47.146 --> 00:01:54.517
Then Mr. Freaky spoke in a low tone. "Who . . . did . . . this?"

26
00:01:54.518 --> 00:01:57.030
Ms. Van Ghoul pushed through the crowd.

27
00:01:57.031 --> 00:01:59.574
"What's going on, Mr. Freaky?"

28
00:01:59.575 --> 00:02:05.335
The principal pointed. Ms. Van Ghoul stepped closer to the poster.

29
00:02:05.336 --> 00:02:10.635
Mr. Freaky took out a handkerchief and blew his noses.

30
00:02:10.636 --> 00:02:17.547
For a second, Ben thought Ms. Van Ghoul might start laughing.

31
00:02:17.548 --> 00:02:23.027
Instead she tilted her head to view the poster from another angle.

32
00:02:23.028 --> 00:02:24.716
"Why, Mr. Freaky.

33
00:02:24.717 --> 00:02:27.505
You look very handsome with a mustache.

34
00:02:27.506 --> 00:02:31.954
Have you ever considered growing one?"

35
00:02:31.955 --> 00:02:35.509
"Did you just say . . . "

36
00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:40.982
A smile crept across his face. " I look handsome?"

37
00:02:40.983 --> 00:02:44.338
"Yes! That's exactly what I said.

38
00:02:44.339 --> 00:02:48.322
A mustache would show off those three beautiful noses!

39
00:02:48.323 --> 00:02:50.727
And don't worry about this prank.

40
00:02:50.728 --> 00:02:52.899
I think it's a good sign.

41
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:57.464
It shows that our artistic juices are flowing for Art Week."

42
00:02:57.465 --> 00:03:01.031
"So . . ." Mr. Freaky was still smiling.

43
00:03:01.032 --> 00:03:06.251
"Does that mean . . . Are you saying that everything is under control?"

44
00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:12.130
"Yes." The art teacher nodded. "Everything is just fine." "Phew!"

45
00:03:12.131 --> 00:03:17.931
Mr. Freaky blew out a breath and put away his handkerchief. "Good!

46
00:03:17.932 --> 00:03:23.328
I can return to the industrial arts classroom then." He laughed shyly. "I'm

47
00:03:23.329 --> 00:03:28.953
actually in the middle of creating an art project myself." "Really?"

48
00:03:28.954 --> 00:03:34.511
Ms. Van Ghoul sounded surprised. "I

49
00:03:34.512 --> 00:03:38.394
used to sculpt while I was in college. I

50
00:03:38.395 --> 00:03:41.920
think you'll find my latest work very, very special. I

51
00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:45.511
plan to unveil it on Wednesday." Abruptly

52
00:03:45.512 --> 00:03:48.249
he spun around. "Okay,

53
00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.535
that's enough. Everyone,

54
00:03:49.536 --> 00:03:51.272
get to class. And

55
00:03:51.273 --> 00:03:54.636
no more drawing on posters!" Monsters

56
00:03:54.637 --> 00:03:57.526
began heading off to class. Ben

57
00:03:57.527 --> 00:03:59.529
hurried over to Mog. "Hey,

58
00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:03.312
Mog, did the Doppel Gang draw that mustache?" Mog

59
00:04:03.313 --> 00:04:07.929
nodded. "I thought it was funny," he said. "And

60
00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:12.557
artistic. It even gave me an idea for an art project." "The

61
00:04:12.558 --> 00:04:16.740
prank was funny, but I wouldn't call it artistic," Ben said. "And

62
00:04:16.741 --> 00:04:20.141
maybe you'd better keep away from the Doppel Gang for a while. I

63
00:04:20.142 --> 00:04:31.913
have a feeling they're going to be very, er, creative this week." ***

64
00:04:31.914 --> 00:04:40.597
The next afternoon, after classes were over for the day, Ben met Waldo along with Winnie and some other witches near the gym.

65
00:04:40.598 --> 00:04:48.147
The witches were all carrying supplies for their flying painting—brooms, paintbrushes, and drop cloths.

66
00:04:48.148 --> 00:04:50.979
Waldo had promised to help with the painting.

67
00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:55.562
Ben was planning to take more notes for his newspaper story.

68
00:04:55.563 --> 00:04:57.686
"We sketched the painting last weekend.

69
00:04:57.687 --> 00:05:01.691
Now we're ready to start adding color," Winnie explained.

70
00:05:01.692 --> 00:05:08.957
"If everybody works really hard today, I think we can finish up by tomorrow or Thursday at the latest.

71
00:05:08.958 --> 00:05:14.175
Then it will be ready by Friday night, when Mr. da Creepy comes."

72
00:05:14.176 --> 00:05:19.286
"Cool, but . . ." Ben looked at the witches' supplies.

73
00:05:19.287 --> 00:05:21.948
"Don't you need paints?"

74
00:05:21.949 --> 00:05:24.884
"We need magic paints," Winnie said.

75
00:05:24.885 --> 00:05:28.968
"Remember? It's a magic painting."

76
00:05:28.969 --> 00:05:34.204
"I mixed the paints yesterday and left them in the gym this morning," Waldo said with a grin.

77
00:05:34.205 --> 00:05:36.744
"Everything should be ready to go."

78
00:05:36.745 --> 00:05:39.001
"Thank you so much, Waldo."

79
00:05:39.002 --> 00:05:42.903
Winnie beamed at the wizard and pushed open the gym doors.

80
00:05:42.904 --> 00:05:48.079
"That sounds . . . Oh no!" She let out a gasp.

81
00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.487
Ben and the others gasped too.

82
00:05:51.488 --> 00:05:56.168
Inside the gym it looked like a colorful tornado had struck.

83
00:05:56.169 --> 00:05:59.908
Cans of paint were spilled all over the floor.

84
00:05:59.909 --> 00:06:05.101
Blobs of paint were splattered on the walls and floating through the air.

85
00:06:05.102 --> 00:06:11.557
A tiny witch named Greta burst into tears. "What a mess!"

